Substitute Ferran Torres struck in the second period of extra-time to edge Spain past a 10-man Argentina and give his side a second World Cup trophy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd151b58-83c3-11f1-bf2a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T224620Z-1742739363-UP1EM7J1R96DZ-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd151b58-83c3-11f1-bf2a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T224620Z-1742739363-UP1EM7J1R96DZ-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f31896a8-83b6-11f1-8f45-0fa873d88c2f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 23:18:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd151b58-83c3-11f1-bf2a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T224620Z-1742739363-UP1EM7J1R96DZ-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg">REUTERS - Kai Pfaffenbach</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Wildfire scorches 12,000 hectares north of Madrid, say Spanish authorities</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260719-wildfire-scorches-12-000-hectares-north-of-madrid-say-spanish-authorities</link><description>
A wildfire raging 100 kilometres north of Madrid has spread, burning more than 12,000 hectares and forcing several hundred people to evacuate, local authorities announced on Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05b17c3c-8388-11f1-83f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-fire-000-C2J48NR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05b17c3c-8388-11f1-83f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-fire-000-C2J48NR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f1c39ea-8388-11f1-9197-8dedb811771e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 15:50:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05b17c3c-8388-11f1-83f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-fire-000-C2J48NR.jpg">AFP - HANDOUT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Kenya’s Rift Valley residents reach breaking point: 'The lake moved into my house’</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260719-kenya-s-rift-valley-residents-reach-breaking-point-the-lake-moved-into-my-house</link><description>
With Kenya’s Lake Baringo and Lake Bogoria rising for months now, following above-average rainfall across the Rift Valley over recent years, this summer has seen them – and the communities around them – reach tipping point. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de966308-811e-11f1-8734-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lake-Baringo-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de966308-811e-11f1-8734-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lake-Baringo-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">063e6dc0-7b83-11f1-8b5f-7fc8d62dffcc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:37:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de966308-811e-11f1-8734-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lake-Baringo-5.jpg">© Environmental and Climate Change Group</source><dc:creator>Anne Macharia in Nairobi</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US launches strikes to 'punish' Iran after troops killed</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260719-us-launches-strikes-to-punish-iran-after-troops-killed</link><description>
The United States said airstrikes on Sunday aimed to "punish" Iran over the first US military deaths since renewed hostilities with the Islamic republic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f1f2762-835a-11f1-ae59-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/iran-US-17july2026-afp-000-C2HY39E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f1f2762-835a-11f1-ae59-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/iran-US-17july2026-afp-000-C2HY39E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ab17b538-8351-11f1-95a4-652be2fcd917</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 09:10:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9f1f2762-835a-11f1-ae59-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/iran-US-17july2026-afp-000-C2HY39E.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>African designer Imane Ayissi redefines luxury on Paris haute couture stage</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260719-african-designer-imane-ayissi-redefines-luxury-on-paris-haute-couture-stage</link><description>
Models stepped on to a Paris runway last week wearing sculptural gowns in African textiles by Imane Ayissi – the first and still the only designer from sub-Saharan Africa to take part in Paris's haute couture shows. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2b718ab8-7eb8-11f1-9111-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9D84RD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2b718ab8-7eb8-11f1-9111-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9D84RD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc8e1e54-7ebd-11f1-8fdc-5581fa219da1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 13:21:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2b718ab8-7eb8-11f1-9111-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9D84RD.jpg">AFP - THOMAS SAMSON</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>The Grand Mosque of Paris, 'part of the French Republic' for 100 years</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260719-the-grand-mosque-of-paris-part-of-the-french-republic-for-100-years</link><description>
Inaugurated 100 years ago this week, the Grand Mosque of Paris is France's longest-serving Islamic place of worship and a landmark for Muslims and non-Muslims alike. From its origins as a tribute to Muslim soldiers who fought in the French army to its present as a centre of moderate Islam, rector Chems-Eddine Hafiz says it has an integral place in France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cbd1080-116f-11f1-a60c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3446566.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cbd1080-116f-11f1-a60c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3446566.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe89ee5a-8024-11f1-b544-a97de1dfa122</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 10:50:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cbd1080-116f-11f1-a60c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3446566.jpg">© AFP - LIONEL BONAVENTURE </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French journalist warns of press freedom crackdown as court revives source hunt</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260719-french-journalist-lavrilleux-disclose-warns-of-judicial-crackdown-as-court-revives-source-hunt</link><description>
A French court has ordered the reopening of an investigation into journalist Ariane Lavrilleux over the highly sensitive "Egypt Papers" investigation, reviving a case that press freedom groups say could have major consequences for the protection of confidential sources in France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f7ebef7a-d770-11ef-b4e2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36UD2WY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f7ebef7a-d770-11ef-b4e2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36UD2WY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">961f8e38-8119-11f1-92a1-57e3f657aba9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 08:32:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f7ebef7a-d770-11ef-b4e2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36UD2WY.jpg">AFP - ANNA KURTH</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Sao Tome president faces party rival in polls</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260719-sao-tome-president-faces-party-rival-in-polls</link><description>
Voters in the Atlantic archipelago of Sao Tome and Principe, regarded as a model of democracy in Africa, will head to polling stations on Sunday for the presidential election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/95b208dc-8334-11f1-a751-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/bd8536f30c867ed30009ab3214dea84c6f730a93.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/95b208dc-8334-11f1-a751-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/bd8536f30c867ed30009ab3214dea84c6f730a93.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96b43f66-8334-11f1-9b22-657ddc83003d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 05:42:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/95b208dc-8334-11f1-a751-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/bd8536f30c867ed30009ab3214dea84c6f730a93.jpg">© CLAUDIA LACAVE / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Saka hits three as England beat France in 10-goal thriller for third place</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260718-saka-hits-three-as-england-beat-france-in-10-goal-thriller-for-third-place</link><description>
Bukayo Saka hit a hat trick as England edged past France 6-4 on Saturday afternoon to claim a zany bronze medal match in Miami.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/695e2996-82fd-11f1-8b47-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/saka.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/695e2996-82fd-11f1-8b47-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/saka.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6b46ef0-82ff-11f1-adce-1fed46e2a2b5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 23:29:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/695e2996-82fd-11f1-8b47-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/saka.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - LUKE HALES</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>The Blue Ridge Mountain mine powering the world’s digital economy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-the-blue-ridge-mountain-mine-powering-the-world-s-digital-economy</link><description>
One of the most abundant minerals in the Earth’s crust, quartz is essential for manufacturing core components of smartphones and computers. Most of the world’s supply comes from a single mining district in the Appalachian Mountains of the southeast United States, which has become an unlikely linchpin of the global tech economy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5168e916-7c72-11f1-9145-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Spruce-Pine-Pegmatite.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5168e916-7c72-11f1-9145-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Spruce-Pine-Pegmatite.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">984c269a-81c7-11f1-95a5-1f0843f75d2d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:02:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5168e916-7c72-11f1-9145-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Spruce-Pine-Pegmatite.png">© Marguliesgm, CC BY-SA 4.0 via Wikimedia Commons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Zimbabwe’s gold rush adds fuel to a deadly surge in malaria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260718-zimbabwe-s-gold-rush-adds-fuel-to-a-deadly-surge-in-malaria</link><description>
In Zimbabwe, open pits left by informal gold miners and filled with stagnant water create breeding grounds for mosquitoes. Health experts say mining is worsening a surge in malaria infections, already spiralling due to funding cuts and climate change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a7e4c1ee-81da-11f1-822a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/A-miner-panning-for-gold-along-Mutare-River-in-Mutasa-Manicaland-Province-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-HEIC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a7e4c1ee-81da-11f1-822a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/A-miner-panning-for-gold-along-Mutare-River-in-Mutasa-Manicaland-Province-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-HEIC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fac7f3e0-81c1-11f1-b1ce-0f8c4be464d3</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 14:28:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a7e4c1ee-81da-11f1-822a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/A-miner-panning-for-gold-along-Mutare-River-in-Mutasa-Manicaland-Province-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-HEIC.jpg">© Farai Shawn Matiashe</source><dc:creator>Farai Shawn Matiashe</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Malawi rolls out injectable HIV prevention drug amid hope and caution</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260718-malawi-rolls-out-injectable-hiv-prevention-drug-amid-hope-and-caution</link><description>
Patrick Chakwana, 50, has lived with HIV since 1999, when there was no effective treatment and the message to those diagnosed was blunt: "Aids kills". Today, as Malawi becomes one of the latest African countries to roll out lenacapavir, a twice-yearly injectable drug that prevents HIV infection, Chakwana's reaction is one of hope, tempered by caution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1f017a70-81f3-11f1-b566-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Thunga-photo-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1f017a70-81f3-11f1-b566-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Thunga-photo-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ccb95e8-81f2-11f1-8d2c-a5cf1b445228</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 10:35:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1f017a70-81f3-11f1-b566-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Thunga-photo-1.jpg">© RFI/ Charles Pensulo</source><dc:creator>Charles Pensulo in Malawi</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US-Iran fighting escalates with infrastructure targeted</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-us-iran-fighting-escalates-with-infrastructure-targeted</link><description>
Iran on Saturday struck infrastructure in the Gulf and threatened a "full-scale offensive" in retaliation for the seventh consecutive night of US strikes on the Islamic republic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f5fe1d8-8227-11f1-96d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/64be5ebe968fbf6d8c93cbaf54b722cd4931a830.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f5fe1d8-8227-11f1-96d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/64be5ebe968fbf6d8c93cbaf54b722cd4931a830.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8ca91d0-82a1-11f1-b21d-b7dd12542a41</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 12:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f5fe1d8-8227-11f1-96d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/64be5ebe968fbf6d8c93cbaf54b722cd4931a830.jpg">© - / US MARINE CORPS/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>France-Morocco rapprochement overshadowed by fresh Pegasus spying claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260718-france-morocco-rapprochement-overshadowed-by-fresh-pegasus-spying-claims</link><description>
As France seeks to rebuild ties with Morocco after years of diplomatic tensions, a new investigation claims Moroccan intelligence targeted senior French officials with Israeli-made Pegasus spyware. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c93201a-81df-11f1-8ec7-d771ed8df869</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:42:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Pogacar wins 'unforgettable' Tour de France 14th stage to extend overall lead</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260718-pogacar-wins-unforgettable-tour-de-france-14th-stage-to-extend-overall-lead</link><description>
Tadej Pogacar won an "unforgettable" mountainous 14th stage of the Tour de France amidst huge crowds in the Vosges on Saturday to extend his lead over Jonas Vingegaard to four and a half minutes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e979a49e-82c0-11f1-82f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/c6ca17b54c5dc358f612844c6f601d29acf1a2ce.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e979a49e-82c0-11f1-82f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/c6ca17b54c5dc358f612844c6f601d29acf1a2ce.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ebe283a-82c3-11f1-892a-792519af272c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:12:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e979a49e-82c0-11f1-82f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/c6ca17b54c5dc358f612844c6f601d29acf1a2ce.jpg">© Anne-Christine POUJOULAT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Syria taken off US terror blacklist after 47 years, paving way for investment</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-syria-taken-off-us-terror-blacklist-after-almost-47-years-paving-way-for-investment</link><description>
Syria is no longer designated a state sponsor of terrorism by the United States – a move that opens the door to American investment in the country, whose economy has been decimated by decades of conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e48e8298-7b30-11f1-b547-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T151203Z-1763665601-RC2R9MALPLGZ-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e48e8298-7b30-11f1-b547-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T151203Z-1763665601-RC2R9MALPLGZ-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5b9f81a2-7ba4-11f1-9a43-45851b99be57</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:11:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e48e8298-7b30-11f1-b547-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T151203Z-1763665601-RC2R9MALPLGZ-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TRUMP.jpg">REUTERS - Jonathan Ernst</source><dc:creator>Anne-Marie Bissada</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>As gang violence expands, Haiti's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-as-gang-violence-expands-haiti-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens</link><description>
Armed gangs in Haiti control nearly all of Port-au-Prince and are expanding their reach outward. Once a peaceful farming community on the outskirts of the capital, the town of Kenscoff has found itself attacked again in recent days – violence that risks worsening food insecurity that the UN warns is already acute.
